"was removed"

#: src/cli.md
msgid "誤りの訳は stderr に 1 行で出る。stdout には、頼んだ物だけが出る。"
msgstr ""
"The reason for an error is printed on stderr in one line. Only what you "
"asked for goes to stdout."

#: src/cli.md
msgid ""
"新しい API には版の header が無く、形の版は定義の release の tag との "
"`smithy diff` が守る（[新しい API の形](next.md) の「共通の決まり」）。それで"
"も code 4 を残すのは、0.8.x の置き場に向けた時に、読めない答えを code 3 とせ"
"ず「違う API の置き場」と分けて出すため。生成した client は、答えに無い "
"`@required` の欄を既定の値で埋めるので、0.8.x の置き場の答えを読ませると、"
"黙って崩れた記録を出してしまう。だから header を、答えを読む前に見る（生成し"
"た client には interceptor で、手の道は答えの頭で）。0.8.x の置き場が無くなっ"
"たら（段 9）、`Pagetray-Api` の見分けは消す。"
msgstr ""
"The new API has no version header, and the shape's version is guarded by "
"`smithy diff` against the model's release tag (\"Common rules\" in [The new "
"API shape](next.md)). Code 4 stays anyway so that, when pointed at a 0.8.x "
"store, the CLI reports \"a store with a different API\" instead of treating "
"the answer as unreadable (code 3). The generated client fills `@required` "
"fields missing from an answer with default values, so reading an answer from "
"a 0.8.x store would silently print broken records. So the header is checked "
"before the answer is read (with an interceptor on the generated client, and "
"on the answer head for hand-written routes). Once no 0.8.x store remains "
"(stage 9), the `Pagetray-Api` check is removed."

#: src/cli.md
msgid "`roster page` との関わり"
msgstr "Relation to `roster page`"

#: src/cli.md
msgid ""
"`roster` を使う project では、担当は `roster page`（put・path・list・delete）"
"を使う。`roster page` は、project・Key・役割・控えの folder・消してよい人とい"
"う `roster` の決まりを持ち、同じ API を呼ぶ。`pagetray` は、その決まりを持た"
"ない道具で、`roster` を通さない場面（人の手元・`roster` の project でない "
"folder）で使う。どちらで置いたページも、同じ置き場に入り、どちらからも探せ"
"る。"
msgstr ""
"In a project that uses `roster`, roles use `roster page` (put, path, list, "
"delete). `roster page` carries the rules of `roster` (project, Key, role, "
"the local copy folder, and who may delete) and calls the same API. "
"`pagetray` is a tool without those rules, used where `roster` is not "
"involved (at a person's terminal, or in a folder that is not a `roster` "
"project). Pages stored with either one go into the same store and can be "
"found from both."

#: src/api.md
msgid "API の仕様（API の版 1）"
msgstr "API specification (API version 1)"

#: src/api.md
msgid ""
"pagetray を呼ぶ側（`roster page` など）が頼ってよい形を書く。ここに書いた形"
"を、前からある呼ぶ側が困るように変える時は、API の版を上げる。"
msgstr ""
"This chapter describes the shapes that callers of pagetray (such as `roster "
"page`) may rely on. Whenever a shape described here is changed in a way that "
"breaks existing callers, the API version is bumped."

#: src/api.md src/next.md
msgid "版"
msgstr "Versions"

#: src/api.md
msgid ""
"`GET /api/version` が `{\"version\":\"0.2.0\",\"api\":1}` を返す。`version` "
"はサーバーの版（`Cargo.toml`）、`api` は API の版。"
msgstr ""
"`GET /api/version` returns `{\"version\":\"0.2.0\",\"api\":1}`. `version` is "
"the server version (`Cargo.toml`); `api` is the API version."

#: src/api.md
msgid ""
"どの答えにも（誤りにも、断った答えにも）header `Pagetray-Api: 1` が付く。呼ぶ"
"側は、頼んだその答えで、API の版が合っているかを見られる。"
msgstr ""
"Every response (including errors and refused requests) carries the header "
"`Pagetray-Api: 1`. Callers can check whether the API version matches from "
"the very response they asked for."

#: src/api.md
msgid ""
"この header が無い答えは、API の版ができる前のサーバー（pagestore 0.1.0）の"
"物。形は API の版 1 と同じ。"
msgstr ""
"A response without this header comes from a server that predates the API "
"version (pagestore 0.1.0). Its shapes are the same as API version 1."

#: src/api.md
msgid "API の版を上げる時・上げない時"
msgstr "When to bump the API version, and when not to"

